                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Definitely one of the hardest games I've ever played. Every time you beat anything(and by beat anything I mean just getting to the next checkpoint, not actually beating shit) there is a moment of short lived but nonetheless intense satisfaction that is tempered somewhat by the fact that you are just moving onto the next torturous task; but still I keep coming back. Started this game years ago, played it for a couple months then rage quit for a couple years, but came back recently and am having more success this time, but my expectations are also different. I don't get pissed anymore. I just realize and accept the fact that any given seemingly small section of a level may take me a week to beat and within that time I will have died at least 50 times--sometimes a couple hundred--and I just dedicate myself to the long game with zen like acceptance of the suffering, and eventually I make it through only to realize that it is once again out of the fat and into the fryer. Personally I love it. I like difficult shit. Not always. I also just like hack and slash blood bath games, first person shooters, and the overall casual experience, but when I am really in the mood to die over and over in pursuit of accomplishments that would humble lesser men, nothing quite scratches that itch like WIngs of Vi.",
